  "description": "Description: This is a web development hackathon where participants are required to build a fully functioning website within the given time frame. The problem statement will be provided at the start of the event. Development Guidelines: The solution must be a fully functional website. Teams are free to use any programming languages, frameworks, and tools, provided they comply with the event's rules as well as problem statement. All development + presentation must be completed within the 12-hour timeframe. Event Rules: Teams must arrive at the venue 30 minutes before the start of the hackathon. The use of pre-built templates or code is strictly prohibited unless explicitly allowed by the organizers. Use of AI Tools: AI chatbots such as ChatGPT may be used only for assistance purposes. However, the use of automated AI agents, autonomous systems, IDE-integrated AI chatbots or any app/AI that can generate complete codes is strictly restricted during the hackathon. Any violation can result in disqualification. Internet access will be provided; however, teams must not engage in any unethical practices like plagiarism or copying solutions from others or hacking can lead to immediate disqualification. All submissions must be original and developed during the hackathon. Any team found violating this rule will be immediately disqualified. Teams are encouraged to bring their own laptops, chargers, and other necessary equipment. Basic amenities like Wi-Fi, power outlets will be provided. All participants must carry valid identification proof (Preferable Student ID card).",
