    "details": "<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This is a web development hackathon where participants are required to build a fully functioning website within the given time frame.</li>\n<li>The problem statement will be provided at the start of the event.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Development Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The solution must be a fully functional website.</li>\n<li>Teams are free to use any programming languages, frameworks, and tools, provided they comply with the event's rules as well as problem statement.</li>\n<li>All development + presentation must be completed within the 12-hour timeframe.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must arrive at the venue 30 minutes before the start of the hackathon.</li>\n<li>The use of pre-built templates or code is strictly prohibited unless explicitly allowed by the organizers.</li>\n<li>Use of AI Tools: AI chatbots such as ChatGPT may be used only for assistance purposes.</li>\n<li>However, the use of automated AI agents, autonomous systems, IDE-integrated AI chatbots or any app/AI that can generate complete codes is strictly restricted during the hackathon. Any violation can result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Internet access will be provided; however, teams must not engage in any unethical practices like plagiarism or copying solutions from others or hacking can lead to immediate disqualification.</li>\n<li>All submissions must be original and developed during the hackathon. Any team found violating this rule will be immediately disqualified.</li>\n<li>Teams are encouraged to bring their own laptops, chargers, and other necessary equipment. Basic amenities like Wi-Fi, power outlets will be provided.</li>\n<li>All participants must carry valid identification proof (Preferable Student ID card).</li>\n</ul>",
